<DocsLayout title="Security architecture" description="CopyPatch v2 uses same-origin routing, plain-text content, roles, and storage-safe token handling.">
  <h1>Security architecture</h1>
  <p class="lead">CopyPatch v2 has one browser origin: the host application's origin. Its embedded API route rejects unsafe requests whose <code>Origin</code> does not exactly match that host.</p>

  <h2>Controls</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Copy is normalized and rendered as plain text.</li>
    <li>Built-in authentication uses an Argon2id passphrase, secure same-site cookie, CSRF token, and persistent rate limiting.</li>
    <li>Host-auth adapters authenticate the user and must verify each mutation.</li>
    <li>Roles distinguish draft editing from publishing.</li>
    <li>Persistence stores hashes for session, CSRF, and rate-limit identifiers.</li>
    <li>Expected revisions protect drafts and publication from silent overwrite.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>Read the repository <a href="https://github.com/Woffluon/CopyPatch/blob/main/docs/threat-model.md">threat model</a> before choosing a deployment and authentication strategy.</p>
</DocsLayout>
